.IX Title "Clownfish::Float 3pm"
.TH Clownfish::Float 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Clownfish::Float \- Immutable double precision floating point number.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&    my $float = Clownfish::Float\->new(2.5);
\&    my $value = $float\->get_value;
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 1
\&    my $float = Clownfish::Float\->new($value);
.Ve
.PP
Return a new Float.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBvalue\fR \- Initial value.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS get_value
.IX Subsection "get_value"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $float\->get_value();
.Ve
.PP
Return the value of the Float.
.SS to_i64
.IX Subsection "to_i64"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $float\->to_i64();
.Ve
.PP
Convert the Float to an integer, truncating toward zero.  Throw an
exception if the value is out of the range of an \f(CW\*(C`int64_t\*(C'\fR.
.SS compare_to
.IX Subsection "compare_to"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $float\->compare_to($other);
.Ve
.PP
Indicate whether one number is less than, equal to, or greater than
another.  Throws an exception if \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR is neither a Float nor an
Integer.
.PP
Returns: 0 if the numbers are equal, a negative number if \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR is
less than \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR, and a positive number if \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR is greater than
\&\f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR.
.SS clone
.IX Subsection "clone"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $float\->clone();
.Ve
.PP
Return a clone of the object.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Clownfish::Float isa Clownfish::Obj.
